<header><p class="st-kicker">other · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Isle of Man</h1><p class="st-meta">1765 CE – present · capital Douglas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A self-governing Crown Dependency in the Irish Sea, with one of the world's oldest continuous parliaments, the Tynwald.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The British crown bought the sovereign rights of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-mann">Lordship of Mann</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-atholl">Duke of Atholl</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/revestment-act-1765">Revestment Act</a> of 1765, mainly to stop smuggling that cost the Treasury duties. The island became a direct possession of the crown, though not part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Man kept its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tynwald">Tynwald</a>, with the elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-keys">House of Keys</a> and the Legislative Council, its own laws and taxes. It grew as a Victorian resort, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-isle-of-man">Douglas</a> as capital from 1869, and hosted internment camps in both world wars. The TT motorcycle races began in 1907. The last native speaker of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manx-language">Manx</a> died in 1974, but the language is being revived.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Since the mid 20th century the Isle of Man has expanded self-government and become an offshore financial centre. It remains a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-dependencies">Crown Dependency</a>, with the UK responsible for defence and foreign relations.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/isle-of-man.jpg" alt="Isle of Man" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: Fry1989 eh? · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Isle_of_Mann.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1765 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Douglas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English, Manx</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Isle of Man</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mannin, Ellan Vannin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1896&amp;focus=isle-of-man" aria-label="Isle of Man on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4581 321 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Isle of Man lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4901 577L4897 579M4901 577L4997 651M4901 577L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4897 579h0M4997 651h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4901 577h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4901 577h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Douglas. <a href="/atlas?year=1896&amp;focus=isle-of-man">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
